tures (Network Researched):**\n  - Integrated `plotly` for interactive candlestick charts visualizing EMA30, Donchian support/resistance, and entry/TP/CL horizontal lines.\n  - Implemented Jack's 5-point technical scoring system (Uptrend, Vol Surge, Consolidation, Breakout).\n  - Added a \"Download CSV\" button for screening results.\n  - Consolidated all tutorials into a clean `st.expander` at the top of the UI.\n- **GitHub & Streamlit Deployment:** Set up the local Git repo, installed GitHub CLI (`gh`), authenticated the user, pushed the code to their repository, and guided them through deploying it as a web app on Streamlit Cloud.\n- **Mobile Optimization:** Tweaked Plotly layouts specifically for iPhone 16 Pro (horizontal top legend, tight margins `l=10, r=50`, `dragmode='pan'`, and `config={'displayModeBar': False, 'scrollZoom': True}`).\n- **Yahoo Finance Bypasses:** Reduced `st.cache_data` TTL from 1 hour to 5 minutes for fresher prices. Added a fake Chrome `User-Agent` to the `requests.Session` used by `yfinance` to prevent Streamlit Cloud IP blocking. Added explicit UI warnings when `yfinance` returns empty data.\n\n## 4. Model Knowledge\n- **Yahoo Finance Cloud Blocking:** Streamlit Cloud IPs get heavily rate-limited/blocked by Yahoo Finance. When blocked, `yf.download()` does *not* throw an exception; it silently returns an empty dataframe (`len(df) == 0`). We handle this by checking `if len(df) < 55:` and displaying a Streamlit warning so the user knows *why* a stock was skipped.\n- **Bursa Malaysia Ticker Formats:** Yahoo Finance relies on the 4-digit numerical code plus `.KL` for Malaysian stocks (e.g., Maybank is `1155.KL`, Public Bank is `1295.KL`). Hardcoding string prefixes (e.g., `MAYBANK.KL`) causes `yfinance` to fail and return no data.\n- **Plotly on Mobile:** Default Plotly charts on Streamlit are terrible on mobile (steals scroll, tiny modebar buttons). Essential fixes used: `config={'displayModeBar': False, 'scrollZoom': True}`, `dragmode='pan'`, and aggressively reduced left/bottom margins.\n- **PowerShell Echo Bug:** Using `echo \"text\" >> requirements.txt` in PowerShell writes the file in UTF-16 LE encoding, which completely breaks `pip install` on Linux/Streamlit Cloud servers. Use proper file writing tools.\n\n## 5. Files and Code\n- **Edited:** `C:/Users/wai_j/.gemini/antigravity/brain/c155f291-512d-4565-8630-f27b8bc949d1/stock_screener.py`\n  - *What/Why:* Extensive UI overhaul. Added Plotly charting, caching optimizations, custom `requests.Session` for YF, mobile formatting, and portfolio JSON logic.\n  - *Current Status:* Just modified locally to replace the `my_top_30` list with accurate 4-digit `.KL` codes.\n- **Edited:** `C:/Users/wai_j/.gemini/antigravity/brain/c155f291-512d-4565-8630-f27b8bc949d1/requirements.txt`\n  - *What/Why:* Created and added `streamlit`, `yfinance`, `pandas`, `numpy`, `requests`, `plotly`.\n- **Viewed (Prior Checkpoint):** `w:/My Drive/ZLibrary/02_To Read/2026/10_JACK INVESTMENT.pdf`\n  - *Relevance:* Dictates the core math for the app (EMA30, 20-day Box Consolidation, Volume * 1.2x, 1:1.5 RR ratio).\n\n## 6. Current Work and Next Steps\n- **Immediate Next Step:** I have just replaced the `my_top_30` Malaysian ticker array in `stock_screener.py` with the correct 4-digit numerical codes (e.g., `1155.KL` instead of `MAYBANK.KL`). You must push this fix to the user's GitHub repository immediately:\n  `git add .` -> `git commit -m \"Fix Bursa Malaysia stock codes\"` -> `git push origin master`\n- **Follow-up:** Once pushed, inform the user that the \"no data\" errors they were seeing for the Malaysian stocks were primarily caused by Yahoo Finance refusing to recognize the English company names. Tell them the cloud app will update in a minute with the corrected codes, which should fix the missing data. Also, ask for feedback on the new mobile chart UI on their iPhone 16 Pro.\n\nYou have the 18 following artifacts written to the artifacts directory:\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_