{"step_index":279,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-24T01:27:56Z","content":"Ah! That is entirely my fault for naming the column `\"Take Profit (TP)\"`. \n\nIn your screenshot, you selected the **\"Turtle Trading\"** strategy from the dropdown. \n\nUnlike the Jack Investment strategy (which sets a hard 1:1.5 Take Profit target *above* your entry price), the **Turtle Trading strategy does NOT use a fixed Take Profit target!** Instead, it uses a dynamic **Trailing Stop** (which tracks the 10-day low). The strategy is to ride the uptrend forever until the price eventually falls below that 10-day low.\n\nBecause I put that 10-day low number under the \"Take Profit\" column, it looked like a hard target that was inexplicably lower than your entry price (e.g., Entry 5.25, TP 4.75), which is super confusing!\n\nI just pushed a quick UI fix for this. Now, whenever you use the Turtle Strategy, the Take Profit column will explicitly say **\"Trailing (< 4.75)\"** so you know it's a dynamic floor you use to exit, not a ceiling target!"}
