{"step_index":299,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-24T04:47:21Z","thinking":"**Prioritizing Tool Specificity**\n\nI'm focusing intently on tool specificity. I've been refining my approach to avoid unnecessary use of bash commands for file creation or appending, opting for dedicated tools like `>` and `>>` respectively. I am also working to use `grep_search` more for searching, rather than general grep commands. I must remember to use the more efficient tools.\n\n\n**Refining Tool Usage**\n\nI'm now integrating explicit tool listing before execution, ensuring the most specific tools are chosen. Specifically, I am focusing on using `ls`, `cat`, `grep`, and `sed` for their respective functions. I will now integrate these learnings into the Tab 2 UI and logic, updating the code to save portfolio data. I'm focusing on the `st.radio` widget, and considering `st.text_area` for ticker input.\n\n\n**Updating Portfolio UI Logic**\n\nI am now focusing on refining the UI elements for portfolio management within Tab 2. I'm leveraging `st.radio` for market selection and considering `st.text_area` to allow for ticker input. I'm focusing on parsing ticker data, including handling of quantity entries alongside ticker symbols. Error handling for incorrect inputs is a key concern.\n\n\n**Implementing Portfolio Saving**\n\nI've implemented a save feature for the portfolio data using `st.data_editor` for dynamic editing, and `to_dict('records')` to save data to a dictionary. A \"Save Portfolio\" button triggers the save, updating my portfolio data. I'm using `st.selectbox` for strategy selection and am parsing the edited DataFrame to extract ticker symbols, entry prices, and quantities for the `parsed_items`. This data will be used by subsequent operations.\n\n\n**Calculating Investment Insights**\n\nI'm now focusing on calculating investment insights using the retrieved data. I'm structuring how I'm handling the ticker data and price entry data and quantities for subsequent calculations. I'm integrating this into my portfolio check loop. I must focus on error checking for insufficient data. I'm also ensuring the code can handle custom entry prices and quantities. Finally, I'm integrating the fee calculations.\n\n\n**Calculating Profit & Loss**\n\nI'm now calculating exit fees, total cost, gross and net values, and ultimately, net profit, incorporating custom entry prices. I'm focusing on ensuring these values are accurately calculated and formatted for display, including percentage calculations. I'm also preparing the data for plotting and displaying the necessary details in the output table.\n\n\n**Formatting Table Outputs**\n\nI'm now focusing on formatting the output table strings correctly. I'm dynamically formatting the strings for 'Current', 'Entry', 'Cut Loss', and 'Take Profit'. For 'Entry', I'm checking if the value is \"N/A\" and if so, not formatting it. Otherwise, I will use `.2f` formatting. For \"Take Profit\", I am using the existing implementation with the trailing text. I'm also removing old keys.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"replace_file_content","args":{"AllowMultiple":false,"Description":"Replace Tab 2 with a Data Editor for portfolio management, include Moomoo fee calculation, and update profit results.","EndLine":430,"Instruction":"Replace everything under `with tab2:` down to the end of the file.","ReplacementContent":"with tab2:\n    st.markdown(\"### Manual / Portfolio Tracker\")\n    market = st.radio(\"Select Market\", [\"US Stocks\", \"Malaysia Stocks\"], key=\"port_market\")\n    \n    st.write(\"Manage your portfolio below. Add your exact quantity to see Moomoo fee estimates & Net Profit.\")\n    df_port = pd.DataFrame(portfolio_data[market])\n    edited_df = st.data_editor(df_port, num_rows=\"dynamic\", use_container_width=True)\n    \n    col1, col2 = st.columns([1, 4])\n    with col1:\n        if st.button(\"💾 Save Portfolio\"):\n            portfolio_data[market] = edited_df.to_dict('records')\n            save_portfolio(portfolio_data)\n            st.success(\"Saved!\")\n            \n    strategy = st.selectbox(\"Select Strategy\", [\"Jack Investment\", \"Turtle Trading (System 1)\"], key=\"port_strat\")\n\n    if st.button(\"🔍 Check Portfolio\"):\n        parsed_items = []\n        with st.spinner(\"Resolving stock names...\"):\n            for _, row in edited_df.iterrows():\n                ticker_raw = str(row.get('Ticker', '')).strip()\n                if not ticker_raw: continue\n                try:\n                    entry = float(row.get('Entry Price', 0.0))\n                    qty = float(row.get('Quantity', 0))\n                except:\n                    entry, qty = 0.0, 0.0\n                parsed_items.append((resolve_ticker(ticker_raw, market), entry if entry > 0 else None, qty))\n                \n        results, charts_data = [], {}\n        progress_bar = st.progress(0)\n        \n        for i, ((ticker, shortname), custom_entry, qty) in enumerate(parsed_items):\n            try:\n                df = fetch_data(ticker)\n                if len(df) < 55: \n                    st.warning(f\"Not enough data for {shortname} ({ticker}). Yahoo Finance might be blocking this Cloud server IP.\")\n                    continue\n                df = calculate_indicators(df)\n                latest = df.iloc[-1]\n                \n                res = analyze_jack_investment(df, latest, custom_entry) if strategy == \"Jack Investment\" else analyze_turtle_trading(df, latest, custom_entry)\n                res['Stock'] = f\"{shortname} ({ticker})\"\n                \n                current_price = latest['Close']\n                if custom_entry is not None and qty > 0:\n                    entry_fees = calc_moomoo_fees(custom_entry, qty, market)\n                    exit_fees = calc_moomoo_fees(current_price, qty, market)\n                    total_cost = (custom_entry * qty) + entry_fees\n                    gross_value = (current_price * qty)\n                    net_value = gross_value - exit_fees\n                    net_profit = net_value - total_cost\n                    net_profit_pct = (net_profit / total_cost) * 100\n                    \n                    res['Qty'] = int(qty)\n                    res['Cost (w/ Fees)'] = f\"{total_cost:.2f}\"\n                    res['Net Profit'] = f\"{net_profit:.2f} ({net_profit_pct:.2f}%)\"\n                else:\n                    res['Qty'] = \"-\"\n                    res['Cost (w/ Fees)'] = \"-\"\n                    res['Net Profit'] = \"-\"\n                \n                # Store raw floats for plotting\n                charts_data[res['Stock']] = (df, res['Entry Price'], res['Take Profit (TP)'], res['Cut Loss (CL)'])\n                \n                # Format strings for the table\n                res['Current'] = f\"{current_price:.2f}\"\n                res['Entry'] = f\"{res['Entry Price']:.2f}\"\n                res['Cut Loss'] = f\"{res['Cut Loss (CL)']:.2f}\"\n                if strategy == \"Turtle Trading (System 1)\":\n                    res['Take Profit'] = f\"Trailing (< {res['Take Profit (TP)']:.2f})\"\n                else:\n                    res['Take Profit'] = f\"{res['Take Profit (TP)']:.2f}\"\n                    \n                # Clean up old keys\n                for k in ['Entry Price', 'Cut Loss (CL)', 'Take Profit (TP)']:\n                    if k in res: del res[k]\n                    \n                results.append(res)\n            except Exception as e:\n                st.error(f\"Error processing {shortname}: {e}\")\n            progress_bar.progress((i + 1) / len(parsed_items))\n            \n        if results:\n            results_df = pd.DataFrame(results)[['Stock', 'Score', 'Status', 'Current', 'Entry', 'Qty', 'Cost (w/ Fees)', 'Net Profit', 'Cut Loss', 'Take Profit', 'TA Summary']]\n            st.dataframe(results_df.style.map(color_status, subset=['Status']))\n            \n            st.markdown(\"### 📊 Interactive Charts\")\n            for stock, (df, entry, tp, cl) in charts_data.items():\n                with st.expander(f\"View Chart: {stock}\"):\n                    st.plotly_chart(plot_interactive_chart(df, stock, entry, tp, cl), use_container_width=True, config={'displayModeBar': False, 'scrollZoom': True})\n        else:\n            st.info(\"No results found.\")","StartLine":303,"TargetContent":"with tab2:\n    st.markdown(\"### Manual / Portfolio Tracker\")\n    market = st.radio(\"Select Market\", [\"US Stocks\", \"Malaysia Stocks\"], key=\"port_market\")\n    tickers_input = st.text_area(\"Your Saved Tickers (comma separated, use @price for entry)\", portfolio_data[market])\n    \n    col1, col2 = st.columns([1, 4])\n    with col1:\n        if st.button(\"💾 Save Portfolio\"):\n            portfolio_data[market] = tickers_input\n            save_portfolio(portfolio_data)\n            st.success(\"Saved!\")\n            \n    strategy = st.selectbox(\"Select Strategy\", [\"Jack Investment\", \"Turtle Trading (System 1)\"], key=\"port_strat\")\n\n    if st.button(\"🔍 Check Portfolio\"):\n        raw_inputs = [t.strip() for t in tickers_input.split(\",\") if t.strip()]\n        parsed_items = []\n        with st.spinner(\"Resolving stock names...\"):\n            for t in raw_inputs:\n                if \"@\" in t:\n                    parts = t.split(\"@\")\n                    try:\n                        parsed_items.append((resolve_ticker(parts[0].strip(), market), float(parts[1].strip())))\n                    except Exception as e: \n                        st.error(f\"Error parsing price for {t}: {e}\")\n                else:\n                    parsed_items.append((resolve_ticker(t, market), None))\n                \n        results, charts_data = [], {}\n        progress_bar = st.progress(0)\n        \n        for i, ((ticker, shortname), custom_entry) in enumerate(parsed_items):\n            try:\n                df = fetch_data(ticker)\n                if len(df) < 55: \n                    st.warning(f\"Not enough data for {shortname} ({ticker}). Yahoo Finance might be blocking this Cloud server IP.\")\n                    continue\n                df = calculate_indicators(df)\n                latest = df.iloc[-1]\n                \n                res = analyze_jack_investment(df, latest, custom_entry) if strategy == \"Jack Investment\" else analyze_turtle_trading(df, latest, custom_entry)\n                res['Stock'] = f\"{shortname} ({ticker})\"\n                \n                # Store raw floats for plotting\n                charts_data[res['Stock']] = (df, res['Entry Price'], res['Take Profit (TP)'], res['Cut Loss (CL)'])\n                \n                # Format strings for the table\n                res['Entry Price'] = f\"{res['Entry Price']:.2f}\"\n                res['Cut Loss (CL)'] = f\"{res['Cut Loss (CL)']:.2f}\"\n                if strategy == \"Turtle Trading (System 1)\":\n                    res['Take Profit (TP)'] = f\"Trailing (< {res['Take Profit (TP)']:.2f})\"\n                else:\n                    res['Take Profit (TP)'] = f\"{res['Take Profit (TP)']:.2f}\"\n                    \n                results.append(res)\n            except Exception as e:\n                st.error(f\"Error processing {shortname}: {e}\")\n            progress_bar.progress((i + 1) / len(parsed_items))\n            \n        if results:\n            results_df = pd.DataFrame(results)[['Stock', 'Score', 'Status', 'Entry Price', 'Cut Loss (CL)', 'Take Profit (TP)', 'TA Summary']]\n            st.dataframe(results_df.style.map(color_status, subset=['Status']))\n            \n            st.markdown(\"### 📊 Interactive Charts\")\n            for stock, (df, entry, tp, cl) in charts_data.items():\n                with st.expander(f\"View Chart: {stock}\"):\n                    st.plotly_chart(plot_interactive_chart(df, stock, entry, tp, cl), use_container_width=True, config={'displayModeBar': False, 'scrollZoom': True})\n        else:\n            st.info(\"No results found.\")","TargetFile":"C:/Users/wai_j/.gemini/antigravity/brain/c155f291-512d-4565-8630-f27b8bc949d1/stock_screener.py","TargetLintErrorIds":[],"toolAction":"Replacing Tab 2 UI","toolSummary":"Redesign Tab 2 UI"}}]}
