{"step_index":303,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-24T04:47:58Z","content":"I have completely redesigned the **\"My Portfolio\"** tab to act as a proper portfolio manager and integrated a **Moomoo Fee Calculator** to track your true net profits!\n\nHere is what I just built and deployed to your app:\n\n### 1. Interactive Portfolio Editor\nI removed the old, clunky text box. Now, there is a slick, editable table right inside the app! \n*   You can dynamically add rows, click into the cells, and type out your **Ticker**, **Entry Price**, and exactly how much **Quantity** (shares) you bought. \n*   Click **\"Save Portfolio\"** and it will memorize all these details across your devices! (I've also built a background migrator so it automatically rescues your old saved tickers).\n\n### 2. Moomoo True Net Profit Calculator\nWhen you click **\"Check Portfolio\"**, the app now runs a full cost analysis based on Moomoo Malaysia's exact fee structures:\n*   **For Malaysia Stocks (Bursa):** It calculates your Entry cost and simulated Exit cost, charging the standard 0.03% Brokerage (Min RM3), RM3 Platform Fee, Clearing Fee (0.03%), Stamp Duty (RM1 per RM1000), and the 8% SST tax on the brokerage/platform fees.\n*   **For US Stocks:** It automatically switches formulas and charges the Moomoo standard 0.99 USD Commission + 0.99 USD Platform Fee + SEC/Settlement fees.\n*   **Net Profit:** The table now includes three brand new columns: **Qty**, **Cost (w/ Fees)**, and **Net Profit**. The Net Profit tells you your *true* dollar value and percentage gain/loss *after* both buying and selling fees are subtracted!\n\nGive the app a refresh, click over to the \"My Portfolio\" tab, punch in how many shares of SUNCON you bought, and see what your true take-home profit is!"}
